                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_54\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix removes an \"if (sourceTrack != null)\" guard around track creation in Util.retargetAnimation() / retargetTrack() and replaces it with logic that synthesizes a single-keyframe bind-pose track when sourceTrack is null, instead of silently skipping the bone track altogether. This is the \"retargeting logic error\": when a source animation has no track for a given bone, the old code simply omitted the target bone's track from the retargeted animation, which is incorrect (it should fall back to the bind pose).\n\nTracing the history of Util.retargetTrack/retargetAnimation across the candidates:\n\n- candidate_36 introduces the original retargetTrack()/retargetAnimation() methods. Here retargetTrack() looks up sourceTrack internally via MyAnimation.findTrack() and immediately calls sourceTrack.getTimes() with NO null check at all \u2014 a latent NullPointerException risk, but no track-skipping behavior yet.\n\n- candidate_54 is the commit that changes this method signature so sourceTrack is now resolved in retargetAnimation() and passed in, and \u2014 critically \u2014 wraps the call to retargetTrack() in `if (sourceTrack != null) { ... result.addTrack(track); }`, silently skipping the target bone's track whenever no matching source track exists. It also adds `Validate.nonNull(sourceTrack, \"source track\")` inside retargetTrack(), reinforcing that null tracks are treated as an error/skip case rather than falling back to bind pose. This is exactly the flawed behavior later corrected by the fix.\n\n- candidate_53 makes only a cosmetic change, appending the comment `// handle null sourceTrack` to the existing `if (sourceTrack != null) {` line introduced in candidate_54; the logic itself is unchanged, so it doesn't introduce new bug behavior.\n\n- candidate_55 is identical to the fix commit itself (removes the null check and adds proper bind-pose fallback), so it is the fix, not the introducing commit.\n\nSince candidate_54 is the first commit to introduce the \"skip track if sourceTrack is null\" logic that the fix commit explicitly reverses, it is the bug-introducing commit.\n"
